## Verifying the AMI

After launching a test instance from your new AMI, verify the services are
running and the health endpoint is accessible:

```bash
# Service status
systemctl is-enabled loreserver
systemctl is-active amazon-ssm-agent

# Health check — must return 200
curl -sf http://localhost:41339/health_check && echo "Health: OK"

# Binary check
which loreserver

# Config directory writable
sudo mkdir -p /etc/loreserver
sudo bash -c 'echo test > /etc/loreserver/local.toml'
```

Then verify Fabrica can build the provisioning plan:

```bash
fabrica lore create --dry-run
```

## Common Pitfalls

| Problem | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| `loreserver` not found | Binary must be on PATH — symlink to `/usr/local/bin/loreserver` |
| Health check fails (41339) | loreserver not running — check `systemctl status loreserver` |
| SSM connection fails | SSM agent must be installed and enabled in the AMI |
| Image Builder rejects the recipe | The placeholder `REPLACE_WITH_CUSTOM_COMPONENT_ARN` was not substituted |
| AMI in wrong region | Re-copy the AMI to each deployment region |
| Architecture mismatch | Build the AMI on the same instance family (x86_64 for m7i) |
